# Convex deployment URL — required for auth (sign-in / sign-up / upload authorization).
# Create a free deployment with `npx convex dev`, then paste the URL here, e.g.:
# VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment-123.convex.cloud
VITE_CONVEX_URL=

# --- AI quiz generation (server-side Worker secrets, NOT VITE_-prefixed) ---
#
# Quizzes are generated by walking a fallback chain of models across seven
# providers, in this order: Meta, AIHubMix, Gemini, Groq, OpenRouter, NVIDIA,
# Comet (see app/lib/ai.server.ts). Each key is read with `env.<NAME>`
# inside the Worker, so none of them may carry the VITE_ prefix — Vite inlines
# VITE_* values into the browser bundle, which would expose the keys to anyone
# who opens DevTools.
#
# Only one key is needed to generate a quiz; the chain skips the models whose
# provider has no key. Set as many as you have. The README's "AI model chain"
# section is the fuller guide.
#
# For `npm run dev`, put the values in `.dev.vars` (see .dev.vars).
#
# For production, pick one. The keys are read at *runtime*, never baked into
# the bundle, so they only need setting once and survive every later deploy.
#
#   1. Manually:
#        npx wrangler secret put MUSECODE_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put GLM_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put AIHUBMIX_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put COMET_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put GROQ_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put NVIDIA_API_KEY
#        npx wrangler secret put OPENCODE_API_KEY   # only if you add an OpenCode row
#
#   2. Via CI — add them as GitHub Actions repository secrets. The deploy
#      workflow pushes them to the Worker after each deploy, so rotating a key
#      is a one-place edit. Any key that is not set is skipped, leaving the
#      existing Worker secret alone.
#
# Meta:       https://api.meta.ai/  (Meta Model API) — Muse Spark 1.3 Contributor
#             leads the chain; its thinking cannot be turned off, so the row
#             carries its own 40s ceiling. See the MODEL_CHAIN note.
# Gemini:     https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GLM:        https://z.ai/  (Z.AI / BigModel) — currently unused, see the
#             commented-out rows in MODEL_CHAIN
# AIHubMix:   https://console.aihubmix.com/
# OpenRouter: https://openrouter.ai/workspaces/default/keys
# Comet:      https://www.cometapi.com/
# Groq:       https://console.groq.com/keys
# NVIDIA:     https://build.nvidia.com/  (NVIDIA NIM)
# OpenCode:   https://opencode.ai/  (Zen) — **paid only, and no row ships**. The
#             free tier refuses any client that is not OpenCode's own and trains
#             on your prompts. The provider is wired, so add a row to MODEL_CHAIN
#             (and CHAIN_LABELS) to use it; the two Muse Spark rows need
#             `endpoint: "responses"`.
# Second Gemini key, tried when GEMINI_API_KEY fails with 401/403 or quota
# exhaustion. Optional; without it Gemini behaves as before.
GEMINI_FALLBACK_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GLM_API_KEY=
AIHUBMIX_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
COMET_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
MUSECODE_API_KEY=
OPENCODE_API_KEY=
